A||N||6||Dan87GT||Passenger door won't open||||1||
Z||000000||Dan87GT||05-22-2000||07:36 AM||||I just got my 86 SE out of storage and the passenger door won't open from the inside or the outside. Any thoughts on how to open?||||reg||1
Z||000001||deceler8||05-22-2000||09:10 AM||||Yeah, I've got three words...<P>Dukes of Hazzard...just have your passenger climb in.<P>Could be as simple as the linkage from the inside lock button having fallen off or jammed in the locked position.<P>The problem is getting the door panel off with the door closed...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dan87GT||05-22-2000||12:09 PM||||That's my problem, I don't see how you can take off the door panel without destroying it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||deceler8||05-22-2000||12:16 PM||||Take off the plastic cover that houses the lock button and door handle and see if you can move the wire piece that operates the lock mechanism...try pulling it to the unlocked position with a pair of needlenose pliers.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bigred||05-22-2000||06:08 PM||||Same thing happened to me.  With a  slim jim and the window all the way down you can see the rods that control the lock. If the rods have slipped out you can still work the mechanism.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||05-24-2000||10:57 AM||||I have a similar problem.  My lock rod will move, but apparently not enough.  I've tried using the key and using pliers, but they didn't seem to work.  Seems like something may be jammed.  Any suggestions???||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||05-24-2000||05:19 PM||||one cause of this is the little plastic clip/bushing thingy wearing out or breaking. they have enough to hold the rod but to much slop the move the arm right.<P>with the window all the way down try the slimjim on the diferant rod ends. If that it too big try 12ga steel rod bent with a hook on the end bent like below. (ignore the periods. they're filler.) You might need to heat the rod to bend it. (You want really stiff rod for this.)<P>.|<BR>.||_|<P>keep the corners square and the bottom flat. then you can push or pull with it.<P>If you can get out the rubber filler at the back end of the glass it will give you some more room. You may have to cut it out then replace it. try directing some spray oil down in there. it could be something is stuck with dirt.<P>also try pushing in hard on the door as you try to open it. that might unload the latch wich might get it to let go. Make sure you push someplace solid. almost anywhere down the rear 3 inches of the door should be ok. thats where the pannel bolts on. slapping the same area hard may also jiggle it loose. Use you open hand not something hard or you'll crack the door skin.<P>worst thing is if it's really unlocked but the latch arm that the door handle rods pull is too worn or bent to pull the locking ear off the latch. That could get real nasty. in that case try working the latch arms directly. you might get just enough exra travel to pop it that you can't get with the door handle.||165.121.80.55||reg||1
